CORE
main.py
--unwind 5

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A context manager __exit__ that returns a truthy value suppresses an
exception raised in the with-body (PLR §8.5), so f() resumes and
returns 42. Exercises the no-'as' with form, the deferred raise
(via with_cleanup_depth), and the __exit__ return-value-driven clear
of __exception_active.
